From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Age of Decomp patch queue <aod-patches@localhost>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 12:58:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] aod: apply the player's volume to the game's audio output

The game plays through IAudioOut, whose SDL gain followed only the game's own
SetAudioOutVolume, so the master volume of the launcher, RecompLauncher and the
in-game menu changed nothing. The gain is now the game's volume times the
player's (0..300 %, live), and two Sound options join it: mute while the game
window is in the background, and an audio buffer of 10, 20 or 40 ms for
outputs that crackle. The AudioOut tests find the SDL headers of the project
toolchain and cover the new gain and device periods.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
